From 37c03ececba66fbc6f1dc88dbc66fd1c3755872a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohit Visavalia <rohit.visavalia@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 19 Aug 2025 05:25:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 064/190] staging: mmi-dptx: Fix incorrect TU calculation

commit 4ece68fb3eb1655f0e4dcf4c67ba8efea6b1666a from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

The current TU calculation divides color_depth by 8 before
multiplication. For 10 bpc and 12 bpc modes this results in 1,
which leads to an incorrect calculation. Reorder the operations
to ensure the correct value is used.

Signed-off-by: Rohit Visavalia <rohit.visavalia@amd.com>
Reviewed-by: Vishal Sagar <vishal.sagar@amd.com>
Message-ID: <20250819122502.1030134-3-rohit.visavalia@amd.com>
State: pending
Signed-off-by: Quanyang Wang <quanyang.wang@windriver.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/staging/xlnx-mmi-dptx/mmi_dp_link.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/xlnx-mmi-dptx/mmi_dp_link.c b/drivers/staging/xlnx-mmi-dptx/mmi_dp_link.c
index acd4d1dcae87..406efbf1d9de 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/xlnx-mmi-dptx/mmi_dp_link.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/xlnx-mmi-dptx/mmi_dp_link.c
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@ void mmi_dp_video_ts_calculate(struct dptx *dptx, int lane_num, int rate,
 		link_clk = 40500;
 	}
 
-	numerator = dptx->selected_pixel_clock * (color_dep / 8);
+	numerator = (dptx->selected_pixel_clock * color_dep) / 8;
 	denominator = (link_rate) * 10 * lane_num * 100;
 	fixp = drm_fixp_from_fraction(numerator * 64, denominator);
 	tu = drm_fixp2int(fixp);
-- 
